refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
mixedsnmp2_getnext stringhostname stringcommunity arraystringobject_id inttimeout-1 intretries-1
The snmp2_getnext function is used to read the value of the SNMP object that follows the specified object_id.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     Now throws a ValueError when the hostname
     contains null bytes or is 128 bytes or longer, when the port is not
     between 0 and 65535, when the community is empty or contains null
     bytes, when the timeout is lower than -1, or when the retries value is
     lower than -1 or greater than 2147483647.
